  a rejected option leaves success True, so the failure is silent unless stderr is read

  Does a rejected option REVERT to the 1e-7 default, or hold the last valid setting?
  Tested on `copper`, whose margin (3.765e-08) is the one the default straddles: solve it
  under column permutations and count how many edge-slots move against the shipped order.
